Duplicate detection: rule j covered by rule i AND rule i covered by rule j → duplicate. Simplest: compute covers(i,j) and covers(j,i); if both → duplicate (report once for the pair, at j). Else if covers(i,j) → shadowed.

Note: only report the first covering i per j to avoid noise.

protoCovers(a,b): a=="" (any) or a==b.

hostCovers(a, b string) bool:
- a=="*" → true
- a==b → true
- if pa, err := netip.ParsePrefix(a); err==nil { if addr, err := netip.ParseAddr(b); err==nil { return pa.Contains(addr) } ; if pb, err2 := netip.ParsePrefix(b); err2==nil { return pa.Contains(pb.Masked().Addr()) && pa.Bits() <= pb.Bits() } }
- false

srcsCover(a, b []string): every s in b has some t in a with hostCovers(t,s). (src aliases are same domain as hosts for coverage purposes.)

portsCover(a, b []tailcfg.PortRange): every range in b is fully contained in union of a. Since both sorted+merged: check each b range has some a range with a.First<=b.First && b.Last<=a.Last.

dstsCover(a, b []CompiledDst): every bd in b has some ad in a with hostCovers(ad.Host, bd.Host) && portsCover(ad.Ports, bd.Ports).

